  "correction_rules": [
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following sharp upward spikes in price (especially when sentiment is neutral or negative).",
    "Adjust forecasts downward if recent history shows persistent mean reversion toward lower levels (e.g., after 3-5 consecutive days of high prices).",
    "Apply a mild downward bias when sentiment is negative (sentiment history includes -0.25 or 0.00 with no recent positive signals).",
    "Increase forecast conservatism in early periods of new sentiment (e.g., first 3-5 days after sentiment shifts from 0.00 to 0.50).",
    "Avoid overreacting to short-term volatility; smooth forecasts using 5-day moving average if price swings exceed 3% from prior day.",
    "If true outcome is consistently below model forecast over 7+ days, reduce forecast by 5-10% to account for model overconfidence."
  ]
}
